Haskell Examples for CS 311
Section on Primitive and Partial Recursive functions

Pairing in Haskell
cantor.hs	Implementation of Cantor pairing function in Haskell

Primitive Recursive Functions (matches course notes):
pr.hs	  	    Basic definitions; evaluator
prcantor.hs	    Primitive recursive pairing
goedel.hs	    Uses Haskell pairing to Goedel number Primitive Recursive Programs
Examples.hs	    Includes solutions to all problems in Homework 8
trace.hs	    Tracing and certifcate checking for Primitive Recursive functions
lecturepr.hs	    A file that imports almost everything but defines nothing... used in demos

Parital Recursive functions (not quite fully caught up with course notes):
mur.hs		    Basic definitions of Partial Recursive (Mu-Recursive) functions
murcantor.hs	    Stale copy of prcantor, building on mur
murgoedel.hs	    Goedel number Partial Recursive functions; halting construction
tracemur.hs	    Stale version of tracing and certificates.  Uses list version, not
		    tree version in current draft of notes.
